@@ -11,6 +11,50 @@ A retry helps when a failure is brief and the request is safe to send twice. It
 is down, because each retry adds load, and when the request changes state, because a second send can
 create a second order or a second charge.
 
+## Retry or fail fast
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Health check exit code 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Response 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is the request a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Retry-After header present?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Wait the Retry-After time" [shape=box];
+    "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [shape=box];
+    "Retry with the same key" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast and fix the request" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast and report" [shape=doublecircle];
+    "Done" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Health check exit code 0?";
+    "Health check exit code 0?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="no"];
+    "Health check exit code 0?" -> "Response 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [label="yes"];
+    "Response 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Fail fast and fix the request" [label="yes"];
+    "Response 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Is the request a POST?" [label="no"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Retry-After header present?" [label="no"];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no"];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast and report";
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Retry-After header present?" [label="yes"];
+    "Retry-After header present?" -> "Wait the Retry-After time" [label="yes"];
+    "Retry-After header present?" -> "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [label="no, not a POST"];
+    "Retry-After header present?" -> "Retry with the same key" [label="no, POST with key"];
+    "Wait the Retry-After time" -> "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [label="not a POST"];
+    "Wait the Retry-After time" -> "Retry with the same key" [label="POST with key"];
+    "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" -> "Done";
+    "Retry with the same key" -> "Done";
+    "Fail fast and fix the request" -> "Done";
+}
+```
+
+A timeout or a 503 on a POST with no idempotency key still means fail fast: the server may have
+processed the request, and a second send can duplicate it.
+
